# 7. TASK API

Admin:

```http
GET    /api/tasks
GET    /api/tasks/:id
POST   /api/tasks
PUT    /api/tasks/:id
DELETE /api/tasks/:id
```

Admin can assign tasks to employees.

Example:

```json
{
  "title": "Create Login Page",
  "description": "Create responsive login page",
  "employeeId": 5,
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "startDate": "2026-09-10",
  "dueDate": "2026-09-15"
}
```

Employee:

```http
GET   /api/tasks/my
GET   /api/tasks/:id
PATCH /api/tasks/:id/status
POST  /api/tasks/:id/comments
```

Employee can only update their assigned tasks.

Employee can change status:

```text
PENDING → IN_PROGRESS → COMPLETED
```

Prevent invalid status transitions.

---

# 8. ATTENDANCE API

Employee:

```http
POST /api/attendance/check-in
POST /api/attendance/check-out
GET  /api/attendance/my
```

Admin:

```http
GET /api/attendance
GET /api/attendance/:employeeId
```

Check-in rules:

* Employee cannot check in twice on the same day.
* Check-out requires check-in first.
* Check-out cannot happen before check-in.
* Automatically calculate working hours.

Example response:

```json
{
  "date": "2026-09-10",
  "checkIn": "09:30",
  "checkOut": "18:00",
  "workingHours": 8.5,
  "status": "PRESENT"
}
```

Support filters:

```text
date
employee
department
status
month
```

---

# 9. LEAVE API

Employee:

```http
POST /api/leaves
GET  /api/leaves/my
GET  /api/leaves/:id
```

Admin:

```http
GET   /api/leaves
GET   /api/leaves/:id
PATCH /api/leaves/:id/approve
PATCH /api/leaves/:id/reject
```

Employee request:

```json
{
  "leaveType": "CASUAL",
  "fromDate": "2026-09-15",
  "toDate": "2026-09-16",
  "reason": "Personal work"
}
```

Automatically calculate number of days.

Admin rejection:

```json
{
  "rejectionReason": "Insufficient leave balance"
}
```

Rules:

* Employee cannot approve their own leave.
* Employee cannot modify an approved/rejected request.
* Validate date ranges.
* Prevent invalid dates.
* Prevent overlapping leave requests.

